{"resource":{"id":"rust-advanced-concepts","title":"Rust — Advanced Concepts","category":"Programming","difficulty":"Advanced","readingTime":"31 min","pages":33,"lastUpdated":"June 2026","tags":["Programming","Rust","Systems"],"heroImage":"https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1451187580459-43490279c0fa?w=1800&q=80","heroSubtitle":"Deep dive into Rust internals — ownership under the hood, unsafe, smart pointers, macros, async runtime, Pin, Send/Sync, memory layout, FFI, embedded, and production engineering."},"toc":[{"id":"objectives","label":"Learning Objectives"},{"id":"s1","label":"1. Ownership Internals"},{"id":"s2","label":"2. Borrow Checker & MIR"},{"id":"s3","label":"3. Unsafe Rust"},{"id":"s4","label":"4. Smart Pointers Deep Dive"},{"id":"s5","label":"5. Macros & Proc Macros"},{"id":"s6","label":"6. Async Runtime Internals"},{"id":"s7","label":"7. Pin, Send, Sync"},{"id":"s8","label":"8. Memory Layout & Repr"},{"id":"s9","label":"9. Compiler Optimizations"},{"id":"s10","label":"10. FFI & Embedded"},{"id":"s11","label":"11. Distributed Systems in Rust"},{"id":"s12","label":"12. Profiling & Production"},{"id":"diagrams","label":"Architecture Diagrams"},{"id":"best","label":"Best Practices"},{"id":"mistakes","label":"Common Mistakes"},{"id":"summary","label":"Summary & Key Takeaways"},{"id":"faqs","label":"FAQ"},{"id":"references","label":"References"},{"id":"disclaimer","label":"Disclaimer"}],"related":[{"title":"Rust — Reference Guide","tag":"Programming","time":"41 min"},{"title":"Rust — Best Practices","tag":"Programming","time":"16 min"},{"title":"Rust — Real-world Case Study","tag":"Programming","time":"19 min"}],"html":"<section id=\"objectives\" class=\"scroll-mt-24 pt-10\"><h2 class=\"text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight sm:text-3xl\">Learning Objectives</h2><div class=\"mt-4 space-y-4 text-foreground/90\">\n        <ul class=\"list-disc space-y-1 pl-5\">\n          <li>Understand what happens under the compiler.</li>\n          <li>Use unsafe correctly and rarely.</li>\n          <li>Write high-performance, production-grade Rust.</li>\n        </ul>\n      </div></section>\n\n      <section id=\"s1\" class=\"scroll-mt-24 pt-10\"><h2 class=\"text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight sm:text-3xl\">1. Ownership Internals</h2><div class=\"mt-4 space-y-4 text-foreground/90\">\n        <p>Ownership is enforced statically — every value has exactly one owner; when it goes out of scope, <code>Drop</code> runs deterministically. There is no runtime GC and no reference counting unless you opt in.</p>\n        <Figure src=\"https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1519389950473-47ba0277781c?w=1400&q=80\" caption=\"Figure 1 — Ownership tree: each value tracked to its unique owner.\" />\n      </div></section>\n\n      <section id=\"s2\" class=\"scroll-mt-24 pt-10\"><h2 class=\"text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight sm:text-3xl\">2. Borrow Checker &amp; MIR</h2><div class=\"mt-4 space-y-4 text-foreground/90\">\n        <p>The borrow checker operates on Mid-level IR (MIR) and Non-Lexical Lifetimes (NLL). Borrows end at last use, not scope end.</p>\n      </div></section>\n\n      <section id=\"s3\" class=\"scroll-mt-24 pt-10\"><h2 class=\"text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight sm:text-3xl\">3. Unsafe Rust</h2><div class=\"mt-4 space-y-4 text-foreground/90\">\n        <p><code>unsafe</code> unlocks raw pointers, FFI, and unions — you still get borrow checking on safe code paths. Encapsulate unsafe in tiny, audited functions.</p>\n        <div class=\"my-3 overflow-hidden rounded-2xl border border-border/60 bg-slate-950 text-slate-100 shadow-sm\"><div class=\"flex items-center justify-between border-b border-white/10 px-4 py-2 text-xs text-slate-400\"><span>code</span></div><pre class=\"overflow-x-auto p-4 text-[13px] leading-relaxed\"><code>unsafe fn get_first(ptr: *const i32) -&gt; i32 { *ptr }</code></pre></div>\n      </div></section>\n\n      <section id=\"s4\" class=\"scroll-mt-24 pt-10\"><h2 class=\"text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight sm:text-3xl\">4. Smart Pointers Deep Dive</h2><div class=\"mt-4 space-y-4 text-foreground/90\">\n        <table class=\"w-full border-collapse text-sm\">\n          <thead><tr class=\"border-b\"><th class=\"p-2 text-left\">Type</th><th class=\"p-2 text-left\">Ownership</th><th class=\"p-2 text-left\">Thread-safe</th></tr></thead>\n          <tbody>\n            <tr class=\"border-b\"><td class=\"p-2\">Box&lt;T&gt;</td><td class=\"p-2\">Unique</td><td class=\"p-2\">If T: Send</td></tr>\n            <tr class=\"border-b\"><td class=\"p-2\">Rc&lt;T&gt;</td><td class=\"p-2\">Shared</td><td class=\"p-2\">No</td></tr>\n            <tr><td class=\"p-2\">Arc&lt;T&gt;</td><td class=\"p-2\">Shared</td><td class=\"p-2\">Yes</td></tr>\n          </tbody>\n        </table>\n      </div></section>\n\n      <section id=\"s5\" class=\"scroll-mt-24 pt-10\"><h2 class=\"text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight sm:text-3xl\">5. Macros &amp; Proc Macros</h2><div class=\"mt-4 space-y-4 text-foreground/90\">\n        <p>Declarative <code>macro_rules!</code> for pattern-based expansion; procedural macros (<code>#[derive]</code>, attribute, function-like) manipulate token streams via <code>syn</code> + <code>quote</code>.</p>\n      </div></section>\n\n      <section id=\"s6\" class=\"scroll-mt-24 pt-10\"><h2 class=\"text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight sm:text-3xl\">6. Async Runtime Internals</h2><div class=\"mt-4 space-y-4 text-foreground/90\">\n        <p>Rust futures are state machines polled by an executor. Tokio schedules them onto worker threads, using cooperative task-yielding via <code>.await</code>.</p>\n      </div></section>\n\n      <section id=\"s7\" class=\"scroll-mt-24 pt-10\"><h2 class=\"text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight sm:text-3xl\">7. Pin, Send, Sync</h2><div class=\"mt-4 space-y-4 text-foreground/90\">\n        <p><code>Pin&lt;P&gt;</code> guarantees a value won't move, needed for self-referential futures. <code>Send</code> means \"safe to transfer across threads\"; <code>Sync</code> means \"&amp;T is Send\".</p>\n      </div></section>\n\n      <section id=\"s8\" class=\"scroll-mt-24 pt-10\"><h2 class=\"text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight sm:text-3xl\">8. Memory Layout &amp; Repr</h2><div class=\"mt-4 space-y-4 text-foreground/90\">\n        <p>Default layout is unspecified — use <code>#[repr(C)]</code> for FFI, <code>#[repr(transparent)]</code> for zero-cost wrappers.</p>\n      </div></section>\n\n      <section id=\"s9\" class=\"scroll-mt-24 pt-10\"><h2 class=\"text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight sm:text-3xl\">9. Compiler Optimizations</h2><div class=\"mt-4 space-y-4 text-foreground/90\">\n        <p>LLVM backend with LTO, inlining, and monomorphization drive Rust's performance. <code>#[inline]</code> is a hint; <code>#[cold]</code> marks error paths.</p>\n      </div></section>\n\n      <section id=\"s10\" class=\"scroll-mt-24 pt-10\"><h2 class=\"text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight sm:text-3xl\">10. FFI &amp; Embedded</h2><div class=\"mt-4 space-y-4 text-foreground/90\">\n        <p><code>extern \"C\"</code> for cross-language calls; <code>no_std</code> for microcontrollers. <code>bindgen</code> generates bindings from C headers.</p>\n      </div></section>\n\n      <section id=\"s11\" class=\"scroll-mt-24 pt-10\"><h2 class=\"text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight sm:text-3xl\">11. Distributed Systems in Rust</h2><div class=\"mt-4 space-y-4 text-foreground/90\">\n        <p>Tonic (gRPC), Axum, and Kafka clients power services at Meta, AWS, and Cloudflare. Prefer message-driven designs and idempotent handlers.</p>\n      </div></section>\n\n      <section id=\"s12\" class=\"scroll-mt-24 pt-10\"><h2 class=\"text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight sm:text-3xl\">12. Profiling &amp; Production</h2><div class=\"mt-4 space-y-4 text-foreground/90\">\n        <p><code>perf</code> + <code>flamegraph</code> for CPU; <code>heaptrack</code> + <code>dhat</code> for memory; <code>tokio-console</code> for async task health.</p>\n        <Figure src=\"https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1518770660439-4636190af475?w=1400&q=80\" caption=\"Figure 2 — Layered profiling: OS → runtime → application.\" />\n      </div></section>\n\n      <section id=\"diagrams\" class=\"scroll-mt-24 pt-10\"><h2 class=\"text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight sm:text-3xl\">Architecture Diagrams</h2><div class=\"mt-4 space-y-4 text-foreground/90\">\n        <div class=\"my-3 overflow-hidden rounded-2xl border border-border/60 bg-slate-950 text-slate-100 shadow-sm\"><div class=\"flex items-center justify-between border-b border-white/10 px-4 py-2 text-xs text-slate-400\"><span>code</span></div><pre class=\"overflow-x-auto p-4 text-[13px] leading-relaxed\"><code>Source → Parser → HIR → MIR → Borrow Check → LLVM IR → Object → Binary</code></pre></div>\n      </div></section>\n\n      <section id=\"best\" class=\"scroll-mt-24 pt-10\"><h2 class=\"text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight sm:text-3xl\">Best Practices</h2><div class=\"mt-4 space-y-4 text-foreground/90\">\n        <ul class=\"list-disc space-y-1 pl-5\">\n          <li>Minimize unsafe surface; audit every block.</li>\n          <li>Prefer typed APIs over stringly-typed configs.</li>\n        </ul>\n      </div></section>\n\n      <section id=\"mistakes\" class=\"scroll-mt-24 pt-10\"><h2 class=\"text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight sm:text-3xl\">Common Mistakes</h2><div class=\"mt-4 space-y-4 text-foreground/90\">\n        <ul class=\"list-disc space-y-1 pl-5\">\n          <li>Assuming <code>#[inline]</code> forces inlining.</li>\n          <li>Confusing <code>Pin</code> with immutability.</li>\n        </ul>\n        <div class=\"my-4 rounded-2xl border-l-4 border-red-500/40 bg-red-500/10 text-red-900 dark:text-red-100 p-4\"><div class=\"flex items-start gap-3\"><div class=\"mt-0.5 shrink-0\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"20\" height=\"20\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" class=\"h-5 w-5\"><path d=\"m21.73 18-8-14a2 2 0 0 0-3.48 0l-8 14A2 2 0 0 0 4 21h16a2 2 0 0 0 1.73-3Z\"/><path d=\"M12 9v4\"/><path d=\"M12 17h.01\"/></svg></div><div class=\"min-w-0 flex-1\"><p class=\"text-sm font-semibold\">Reminder</p><div class=\"mt-1 text-sm\">Undefined behavior in unsafe compromises the whole program.</div></div></div></div>\n      </div></section>\n\n      <section id=\"summary\" class=\"scroll-mt-24 pt-10\"><h2 class=\"text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight sm:text-3xl\">Summary &amp; Key Takeaways</h2><div class=\"mt-4 space-y-4 text-foreground/90\">\n        <p>Advanced Rust rewards curiosity — the compiler is a lifelong teacher.</p>\n      </div></section>\n\n      <section id=\"faqs\" class=\"scroll-mt-24 pt-10\"><h2 class=\"text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight sm:text-3xl\">FAQ</h2><div class=\"mt-4 space-y-4 text-foreground/90\">\n        <details class=\"group my-2 rounded-2xl border border-border/60 bg-card p-4 open:shadow-sm\"><summary class=\"flex cursor-pointer list-none items-center justify-between gap-4 text-sm font-semibold\"><span>Should I write my own executor?</span><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" class=\"h-4 w-4 shrink-0 transition group-open:rotate-90\"><path d=\"m9 18 6-6-6-6\"/></svg></summary><div class=\"mt-3 text-sm text-muted-foreground\">Rarely — start with Tokio; roll your own only for exotic constraints.</div></details>\n      </div></section>\n\n      <section id=\"references\" class=\"scroll-mt-24 pt-10\"><h2 class=\"text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight sm:text-3xl\">References</h2><div class=\"mt-4 space-y-4 text-foreground/90\"><References /></div></section>\n\n      <section id=\"disclaimer\" class=\"scroll-mt-24 pt-10\"><h2 class=\"text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight sm:text-3xl\">Disclaimer</h2><div class=\"mt-4 space-y-4 text-foreground/90\">\n        <p class=\"text-sm text-muted-foreground\">Advanced APIs evolve; verify against current Rust edition.</p>\n      </div></section>"}